{"authored" [{"question" "q-13944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/assets/7a70285258e584708a7296a2a008536dec9c97750b48e5fe0eb2f8cb7761bed1.png)\n\nCalculate the area of the parallelogram in the figure." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-13944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨3,2⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨2,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-10\\,|=10\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-13944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c2fd1b7355fa6c287086552bf692aa77ee3f50f827fa5efe6bbbbfbe23883039" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/De