ation" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =15-2 \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,13\\,|=13\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c2fd1b7355fa6c287086552bf692aa77ee3f50f827fa5efe6bbbbfbe23883039" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320402" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320402" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{2})\\cdot 6-a\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{2}-3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12\\sqrt{2}-3a & =0 \\\\ -3a & =-12\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c2fd1b7355fa6c287086552bf692aa77ee3f50f827fa5efe6bbbbfbe23883039" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/state.json" "file_sha256" "9ec084eec6c9aa6624842d78db1774daef378db09bd606aea5a93a0b72890d48" "basis" 647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "4292f151be1765de04a1018fa5eed494bc3f3018d87ba134b2b4ee95c91d0a34" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "4292f151be1765de04a1018fa5eed494bc3f3018d87ba134b2b4ee95c91d0a34" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71a94be75fc9bf89f92e07f1bcc70a5c4dc33378bc2c8d6da1b46c650a6c7dae" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "4292f151be1765de04a1018fa5eed494bc3f3018d87ba134b2b4ee95c91d0a34" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "4292f151be1765de04a1018fa5eed494bc3f3018d87ba134b2b4ee95c91d0a34" "basis" 665 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "sele