\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3-5\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,23\\,|=23\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-13951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de8a3787a199968123220fff16e5e1dc1feab2878bffd8d7a7d780bfd9195179"} {"question" "q-13951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-13951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "23"] ["math" "38"] ["math" "52"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-13951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-13944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/assets/7a70285258e584708a7296a2a008536dec9c97750b48e5fe0eb2f8cb7761bed1.png)\n\nCalculate the area of the parallelogram in the figure." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-13944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨3,2⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨2,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-10\\,|=10\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-13944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de8a3787a199968123220fff16e5e1dc1feab2878bffd8d7a7d780bfd9195179"} {"question" "q-13944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-13944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-13944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de8a3787a199968123220fff16e5e1dc1feab2878bffd8d7a7d780bfd9195179"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}+3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} & a \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} & a \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{7})(-10)-a\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{7}-5a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\sqrt{7}-5a & =0 \\\\ 5a & =10\\sqrt{7} \\\\ a & =2\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de8a3787a199968123220fff16e5e1dc1feab2878bffd8d7a7d780bfd9195179"} {"question" "q-320558" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320558" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{2})\\cdot 6-a\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{2}-3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12\\sqrt{2}-3a & =0 \\\\ -3a & =-12\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de8a3787a199968123220fff16e5e1dc1feab2878bffd8d7a7d780bfd9195179"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320557" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=⟨-2,3⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨4,-6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12-12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de8a3787a199968123220fff16e5e1dc1feab2878bffd8d7a7d780bfd9195179"} {"question" "q-69938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-69938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=⟨3\\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{5}⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨a,\\,10⟩$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 10-a\\cdot (-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =30\\sqrt{2}+a\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30\\sqrt{2}+a\\sqrt{5} & =0 \\\\ a\\sqrt{5} & =-30\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{10}}{5} \\\\ a & =-6\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "de8a3787a199968123220fff16e5e1dc1feab2878bffd8d7a7d780bfd9195179"} {"question" "q-320556" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "q-320556" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6\\sqrt{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbe2719c92ef7ff41bff47f6a4d5e89da62e639e7f2425811ea9e91ce66b507c"} {"question" "e-4437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\textbf{u}=\\langle 1,2 \\rangle$ and $\\textbf{v}=\\langle 3, -3 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/example-4437.json" "file_sha256" "821d2c02318519f78bc49769c27ddd3a372a9cb747fd105efa84c692d4f8cd9c"} {"question" "e-4437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/assets/f4b59236b774117dfc764389f3525a01c5f4c8429cece16552622f54cfb3d863.png)\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-3)-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $\\det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA = |{-9}| = 9\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/example-4437.json" "file_sha256" "821d2c02318519f78bc49769c27ddd3a372a9cb747fd105efa84c692d4f8cd9c"} {"question" "e-4438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\textbf{u}=\\langle 3,-2 \\rangle$ and $\\textbf{v}=\\langle 6, -4 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/example-4438.json" "file_sha256" "d56ea64a6f2c100a0f5e44e35daaaf41774cef71eec9fa07a3356779b05f8700"} {"question" "e-4438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/assets/b25d71fb75afcb5e4f9e8ce137ec69fb1dfda54aa544b1636e11503273527844.png)\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-4)-6\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $\\det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA = |\\,0\\,| = 0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/line